    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Here's a video to show what I'm describing: \r\n\r\nhttps://user-images.githubusercontent.com/86020820/217321116-fb8a13f0-5db1-4298-bae5-97839c3b53fd.mov\r\n\r\nIs there any way to prevent the black background from showing up for several seconds? When I disable the plugin, I don't have this issue. ",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Here's a video to show what I'm describing:</p>\n<details open=\"\" class=\"details-reset border rounded-2\">\n  <summary class=\"tmp-px-3 py-2\">\n    <svg aria-hidden=\"true\" data-component=\"Octicon\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" data-view-component=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-device-camera-video\">\n    <path d=\"M16 3.75v8.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.136.643L11 10.575v.675A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 9.25 13h-7.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 0 11.25v-6.5C0 3.784.784 3 1.75 3h7.5c.966 0 1.75.784 1.75 1.75v.675l3.864-2.318A.75.75 0 0 1 16 3.75Zm-6.5 1a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25h-7.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v6.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h7.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-6.5ZM11 8.825l3.5 2.1v-5.85l-3.5 2.1Z\"></path>\n</svg>\n    <span class=\"m-1\">Screen.Recording.2023-02-07.at.12.33.36.PM.mov</span>\n    <span class=\"dropdown-caret\"></span>\n  </summary>\n\n  <video src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/86020820/217321116-fb8a13f0-5db1-4298-bae5-97839c3b53fd.mov?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..iMAkHwf-vzlABMK8Sr2YAfXmiNwbJcbQp_-HiKSWb3k\" data-canonical-src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/86020820/217321116-fb8a13f0-5db1-4298-bae5-97839c3b53fd.mov?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..iMAkHwf-vzlABMK8Sr2YAfXmiNwbJcbQp_-HiKSWb3k\" controls=\"controls\" muted=\"muted\" class=\"d-block rounded-bottom-2 border-top width-fit\" style=\"max-height:640px; min-height: 200px\">\n\n  </video>\n</details>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is there any way to prevent the black background from showing up for several seconds? When I disable the plugin, I don't have this issue.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Here's a video to show what I'm describing:\n\n  \n    \n    \n\n    Screen.Recording.2023-02-07.at.12.33.36.PM.mov\n    \n  \n\n  \n\n  \n\n\nIs there any way to prevent the black background from showing up for several seconds? When I disable the plugin, I don't have this issue.",
