                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                        "login": "echasnovski",
                        "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                        "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "It is possible to animate using window effects with [`gen_winconfig`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/301ee9f3afa2224b833de7c182574ba6c61e8c6e/doc/mini-animate.txt#L800) and adjust `winblend` option to be constant. Here is [an example](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/301ee9f3afa2224b833de7c182574ba6c61e8c6e/doc/mini-animate.txt#L415-L441).\r\n\r\nAnother approach might be to set `MiniAnimateNormalFloat` highlight groups to not have transparent background. Not sure if that will help, though (can't remember and it might depend on how transparent background is set up).\r\n\r\nBut my personal suggestion would be to disable open/close animations altogether if you use transparent background.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">It is possible to animate using window effects with <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/301ee9f3afa2224b833de7c182574ba6c61e8c6e/doc/mini-animate.txt#L800\"><code class=\"notranslate\">gen_winconfig</code></a> and adjust <code class=\"notranslate\">winblend</code> option to be constant. Here is <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/301ee9f3afa2224b833de7c182574ba6c61e8c6e/doc/mini-animate.txt#L415-L441\">an example</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Another approach might be to set <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniAnimateNormalFloat</code> highlight groups to not have transparent background. Not sure if that will help, though (can't remember and it might depend on how transparent background is set up).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">But my personal suggestion would be to disable open/close animations altogether if you use transparent background.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "It is possible to animate using window effects with gen_winconfig and adjust winblend option to be constant. Here is an example.\nAnother approach might be to set MiniAnimateNormalFloat highlight groups to not have transparent background. Not sure if that will help, though (can't remember and it might depend on how transparent background is set up).\nBut my personal suggestion would be to disable open/close animations altogether if you use transparent background.",
